[00:13.75]Once a realm on the shoulders of giants
[00:18.41]Forged with ember and gold
[00:22.45]An empire stood through the clouds, it was endless
[00:27.47]Stories of peace it foretold
[00:31.04]
[00:31.55]Where sea meets sky, emerald water in moonlight
[00:36.64]Mountain tops kissed with snow
[00:41.22]People held up the legends of bounty
[00:45.92]Reaping the peace that they sowed
[00:49.55]
[00:51.08]But one by one, in secret, planted greed
[01:00.18]And watered it with pride and fear
[01:06.44]
[01:08.88]Seasons changed, like the turning of tides
[01:12.97]The blossoms started to fade
[01:17.69]The air grew heavy, electric in warning
[01:22.64]The greedy knelt down and they prayed
[01:26.57]
[01:26.79]They begged for peace, for the legends of bounty
[01:32.13]No one planted or sowed
[01:36.21]The secrets grew like the storm in the distance
[01:41.27]Came to collect what they owed
[01:44.92]
[01:46.43]But one by one, in secret, planted greed
[01:55.57]And watered it with pride and fear
[02:04.79]The poisoned fruit fell not far from the tree
[02:14.17]The fiend that nobody could see
[02:20.83]
[02:22.79]Once a realm on the shoulders of giants
[02:27.53]Forged with ember and gold
[02:32.00]Now a lost land, it’s fading in silence
[02:36.69]Haunted by demons and ghosts
